🕒 What is TimeUtils?
TimeUtils is a utility class designed to simplify time-related operations in Minecraft plugin development. Since Minecraft operates in ticks (where 1 second = 20 ticks), dealing with delays, cooldowns, and timers often requires constant conversions.

This class helps you:

- Convert between seconds, minutes, and ticks

- Format time nicely (e.g., "2m 30s")

- Parse formatted time strings back into ticks

💡 Why Use It?
When you're scheduling tasks, creating cooldowns, or displaying countdowns, working with ticks directly can be error-prone and hard to read.
TimeUtils makes your code cleaner, easier to understand, and less repetitive.

✅ Examples
TimeUtils.secondsToTicks(10);         // ➤ 200 ticks
TimeUtils.formatTicks(280);           // ➤ "14s"
TimeUtils.parseFormattedTime("1m");   // ➤ 1200 ticks

You can also use it to delay events:

Bukkit.getScheduler().runTaskLater(plugin, () -> {
    player.sendMessage("Boom!");
}, TimeUtils.secondsToTicks(5)); // 5-second delay
